00:44:30.786 --> 00:44:31.666
Who is there?

00:44:31.666 --> 00:44:34.066
Senate President Thomas Rivera Schatz,

00:44:34.066 --> 00:44:36.306
former Governor Pedro Pierluisi,

00:44:36.306 --> 00:44:37.666
and the current Health Secretary,

00:44:37.666 --> 00:44:38.706
Victor Ramos,

00:44:38.706 --> 00:44:39.986
all converged on the site

00:44:39.986 --> 00:44:41.186
to inspect the progress.

00:44:41.186 --> 00:44:42.706
And what came out of that visit?

00:44:42.706 --> 00:44:44.866
Well, to report impartially on it,

00:44:44.866 --> 00:44:46.786
Secretary Ramos strongly defended

00:44:46.786 --> 00:44:48.546
the administration's progress.

00:44:48.546 --> 00:44:50.466
He highlighted a significant victory.

00:44:51.186 --> 00:44:53.666
A new modern CT scanner

00:44:53.666 --> 00:44:54.946
had just arrived on the island

00:44:54.946 --> 00:44:55.746
the day before.

00:44:55.746 --> 00:44:56.706
That's a big deal.

00:44:56.706 --> 00:44:57.746
It was a critical point

00:44:57.746 --> 00:44:59.026
because it rectified

00:44:59.026 --> 00:45:01.186
a highly criticized past issue

00:45:01.186 --> 00:45:02.706
where a mobile CT unit

00:45:02.706 --> 00:45:04.146
was purchased for the island.

00:45:04.146 --> 00:45:05.106
But it was just left sitting

00:45:05.106 --> 00:45:06.866
in a warehouse on the main island

00:45:06.866 --> 00:45:08.946
until this warranty completely expired.

00:45:08.946 --> 00:45:09.906
Oh, man.

00:45:09.906 --> 00:45:10.626
Yeah.

00:45:10.626 --> 00:45:12.226
But Secretary Ramos maintained

00:45:12.226 --> 00:45:13.186
during the visit

00:45:13.186 --> 00:45:14.066
that they are targeting

00:45:14.066 --> 00:45:15.666
a late September inauguration

00:45:15.666 --> 00:45:17.746
pending final equipment deliveries,

00:45:17.746 --> 00:45:18.466
health inspections,

00:45:18.466 --> 00:45:19.426
and crucially,

00:45:19.426 --> 00:45:21.586
that complex licensure process.

00:45:21.586 --> 00:45:23.026
It's a perfect analogy.

00:45:23.026 --> 00:45:24.306
The facility right now

00:45:24.306 --> 00:45:25.506
is like a brand new

00:45:25.506 --> 00:45:26.706
fully-fueled jet

00:45:26.706 --> 00:45:27.906
sitting on the runway.

00:45:27.906 --> 00:45:29.026
The engines are humming.

00:45:29.026 --> 00:45:30.146
The private sector pilots

00:45:30.146 --> 00:45:31.106
are ready to get in the seats.

00:45:31.106 --> 00:45:32.626
The passengers are waiting,

00:45:32.626 --> 00:45:34.146
but the plane cannot take off

00:45:34.146 --> 00:45:35.186
because they are just waiting

00:45:35.186 --> 00:45:36.226
for the control tower

00:45:36.226 --> 00:45:37.666
to hand over the final

00:45:37.666 --> 00:45:39.346
stamp registration papers.

00:45:39.346 --> 00:45:40.866
That's exactly where they are.

00:45:40.866 --> 00:45:42.786
The high-profile political visit

00:45:42.786 --> 00:45:45.426
just underscores the intense oversight

00:45:45.426 --> 00:45:47.666
required to push the bureaucracy forward.

00:45:48.546 --> 00:45:50.066
Every single day,

00:45:50.066 --> 00:45:51.826
this building sits classified

00:45:51.826 --> 00:45:54.466
as a CDT or remains unopened.

00:45:54.466 --> 00:45:56.306
The island misses the opportunity

00:45:56.386 --> 00:45:57.506
to start the clock

00:45:57.506 --> 00:45:59.026
on this multi-million dollar

00:45:59.026 --> 00:46:00.066
financial lever.

00:46:00.066 --> 00:46:01.586
Which brings us to the final

00:46:01.586 --> 00:46:03.026
and perhaps most daunting

00:46:03.026 --> 00:46:04.066
logistical challenge

00:46:04.066 --> 00:46:05.266
of this entire endeavor.

00:46:05.986 --> 00:46:07.186
The timeline lag.

00:46:07.186 --> 00:46:08.466
The time delay, yes.

00:46:08.466 --> 00:46:10.146
Because even if the Department of Health

00:46:10.146 --> 00:46:11.346
signs the hospital license

00:46:11.346 --> 00:46:12.306
tomorrow morning

00:46:12.306 --> 00:46:14.066
and the facility opens fully staffed

00:46:14.066 --> 00:46:15.666
paying $30 an hour,

00:46:15.666 --> 00:46:16.546
the spreadsheet

00:46:16.546 --> 00:46:18.146
does not update overnight.

00:46:18.146 --> 00:46:19.586
Right, because federal bureaucracy

00:46:19.586 --> 00:46:20.786
is never instantaneous.

00:46:20.786 --> 00:46:22.706
There is a built-in time delay.

00:46:22.706 --> 00:46:23.906
Walk us through the clock on this.

00:46:23.906 --> 00:46:25.666
Why doesn't the money flow immediately?

00:46:25.666 --> 00:46:28.066
Because Medicare builds its wage index

00:46:28.066 --> 00:46:29.986
using audited cost reports.

00:46:29.986 --> 00:46:31.986
And those reports are, by definition,

00:46:31.986 --> 00:46:32.786
historical.

00:46:32.786 --> 00:46:33.506
Right.

00:46:33.506 --> 00:46:34.626
It takes time for a hospital

00:46:34.626 --> 00:46:36.146
to finish a fiscal year,

00:46:36.146 --> 00:46:37.666
compile their payroll data,

00:46:37.666 --> 00:46:39.186
file the complex report,

00:46:39.186 --> 00:46:41.186
have an independent auditor review it,

00:46:41.186 --> 00:46:43.106
and then have CMS actually integrate

00:46:43.106 --> 00:46:44.066
that data

00:46:44.066 --> 00:46:45.426
into the massive national

00:46:45.426 --> 00:46:46.546
rule-making cycle.

00:46:47.586 --> 00:46:48.386
Generally speaking,

00:46:48.386 --> 00:46:50.066
the wage index is based on data

00:46:50.066 --> 00:46:52.226
that is roughly four years old.

00:46:52.226 --> 00:46:53.026
Four years.

00:46:53.026 --> 00:46:54.386
Okay, let's play this timeline out

00:46:54.386 --> 00:46:56.706
so we really understand the gap here.

00:46:56.706 --> 00:46:58.626
If the VX hospital opens

00:46:58.626 --> 00:47:00.706
and is certified as an IPPS hospital

00:47:00.706 --> 00:47:02.706
in fiscal year 2027.

00:47:02.706 --> 00:47:04.706
It's high wages wouldn't actually hit

00:47:04.706 --> 00:47:06.706
the published operational wage index

00:47:06.706 --> 00:47:08.706
until fiscal year 2031.

00:47:08.706 --> 00:47:10.066
So the San Juan hospitals wouldn't

00:47:10.066 --> 00:47:12.226
see the benefit until 2031.

00:47:12.226 --> 00:47:12.866
Yes.

00:47:12.866 --> 00:47:13.426
And remember,

00:47:13.426 --> 00:47:14.546
the repricing mechanism

00:47:14.546 --> 00:47:15.346
for Medicare Advantage

00:47:15.346 --> 00:47:16.226
we discussed earlier.

00:47:16.226 --> 00:47:16.946
Oh, right.

00:47:16.946 --> 00:47:17.426
The AGAs.

00:47:17.426 --> 00:47:19.106
Do you know how the AGAs calculated?

00:47:19.106 --> 00:47:21.746
That adds roughly another calendar year of delay.

00:47:21.746 --> 00:47:23.346
So those higher wages from VX

00:47:23.346 --> 00:47:25.106
wouldn't fully hit and stabilize

00:47:25.106 --> 00:47:26.866
the Medicare Advantage benchmarks

00:47:26.866 --> 00:47:28.866
until calendar year 2032.

00:47:28.866 --> 00:47:31.186
Okay, 2032 is the finish line,

00:47:31.826 --> 00:47:33.586
but the 5% cuts from the bridgeport

00:47:33.586 --> 00:47:35.266
ruling are happening right now.

00:47:35.266 --> 00:47:35.986
Exactly.

00:47:35.986 --> 00:47:40.226
The 5% cuts for 2025, 2026, and 2027

00:47:40.226 --> 00:47:42.226
are already cascading through the system,

00:47:42.226 --> 00:47:43.346
cutting revenue today.

00:47:43.906 --> 00:47:46.626
The calendar year 2028 Medicare Advantage

00:47:46.626 --> 00:47:47.666
benchmarks,

00:47:47.666 --> 00:47:49.586
which are currently being formulated,

00:47:49.586 --> 00:47:52.146
already have those compounding cuts locked in.

00:47:52.146 --> 00:47:52.946
Wow.

00:47:52.946 --> 00:47:55.266
So there is a definitive four-year gap

00:47:55.266 --> 00:47:57.906
from roughly 2028 to 2032

00:47:58.466 --> 00:48:00.546
where the VX data hasn't ripened yet,

00:48:00.546 --> 00:48:01.586
but the bridgeport cuts

00:48:01.586 --> 00:48:03.506
are fully active and accelerating.

00:48:03.506 --> 00:48:04.706
The island's healthcare system

00:48:04.706 --> 00:48:06.306
will bleed millions of dollars

00:48:06.306 --> 00:48:07.826
significantly during that window.

00:48:07.826 --> 00:48:09.426
So how do they survive the gap?

00:48:09.426 --> 00:48:10.706
You can't just tell an ICU

00:48:10.706 --> 00:48:12.306
to hold its breath for four years

00:48:12.306 --> 00:48:14.306
while waiting for a spreadsheet to update.

00:48:14.306 --> 00:48:15.746
This raises an important question

00:48:15.746 --> 00:48:17.906
about how you enact durable systemic change.

00:48:17.906 --> 00:48:18.866
You cannot just rely

00:48:18.866 --> 00:48:20.946
on the geographic solution on the ground.

00:48:20.946 --> 00:48:22.386
You have to run a parallel track

00:48:22.466 --> 00:48:24.946
of intense administrative advocacy in Washington.

00:48:24.946 --> 00:48:25.986
The island needs to show up

00:48:25.986 --> 00:48:26.866
in the federal docket

00:48:26.866 --> 00:48:27.986
and fight for a bridge.

00:48:27.986 --> 00:48:28.786
They do.

00:48:28.786 --> 00:48:30.066
And the docket participation

00:48:30.066 --> 00:48:32.306
is a shockingly weak point right now.

00:48:32.306 --> 00:48:33.266
This is a statistic

00:48:33.266 --> 00:48:34.786
that absolutely floored me

00:48:34.786 --> 00:48:36.306
when we were researching this.

00:48:36.306 --> 00:48:39.586
When CMS published the fiscal year 2027

00:48:39.586 --> 00:48:41.506
IPPS proposed rule,

00:48:41.506 --> 00:48:42.626
the specific rule

00:48:42.626 --> 00:48:44.626
that executed the third consecutive

00:48:44.626 --> 00:48:47.266
5% cut to Puerto Rico's hospitals,

00:48:47.266 --> 00:48:49.826
there were 982 public comments

00:48:49.826 --> 00:48:51.506
filed nationally by hospitals,

00:48:51.506 --> 00:48:53.106
associations and advocates.

00:48:53.106 --> 00:48:55.586
982 comments across the country.

00:48:55.586 --> 00:48:58.066
Do you know how many of those 982 comments

00:48:58.066 --> 00:49:00.146
came from institutions in Puerto Rico

00:49:00.146 --> 00:49:01.106
fighting the cut?

00:49:01.106 --> 00:49:01.666
Four.

00:49:01.666 --> 00:49:03.666
Four out of nearly a thousand.

00:49:03.666 --> 00:49:04.946
Four comments representing

00:49:04.946 --> 00:49:06.066
an entire territory

00:49:06.066 --> 00:49:07.346
facing a financial crisis.

00:49:07.346 --> 00:49:08.146
It's unbelievable.

00:49:08.146 --> 00:49:10.546
You simply cannot win a bureaucratic war

00:49:10.546 --> 00:49:11.506
if you do not show up

00:49:11.506 --> 00:49:13.186
on the administrative battlefield.

00:49:13.186 --> 00:49:14.866
The hospitals, the associations,

00:49:14.866 --> 00:49:15.586
the public,

00:49:15.586 --> 00:49:17.346
they absolutely must mobilize

00:49:17.346 --> 00:49:18.626
to comment on the upcoming

00:49:18.626 --> 00:49:20.866
FY 2028 proposed rule.

00:49:20.946 --> 00:49:22.786
Explicitly asking CMS to use

00:49:22.786 --> 00:49:24.066
its administrative discretion

00:49:24.066 --> 00:49:25.906
to hold or pause the transition cuts

00:49:25.906 --> 00:49:27.986
while the new VX wage data matures.

00:49:27.986 --> 00:49:29.426
And there is a secondary,

00:49:29.426 --> 00:49:30.466
highly specific,

00:49:30.466 --> 00:49:32.546
statutory channel available as well.

00:49:33.506 --> 00:49:35.346
Under section 1853

00:49:35.346 --> 00:49:36.946
of the Social Security Act,

00:49:36.946 --> 00:49:38.306
the governor of a territory

00:49:38.306 --> 00:49:40.226
has a formal legal mechanism

00:49:40.226 --> 00:49:41.426
to request adjustments

00:49:41.426 --> 00:49:43.666
to the Medicare Advantage payment methodology

00:49:43.666 --> 00:49:44.786
directly from the Secretary

00:49:44.786 --> 00:49:46.226
of Health and Human Services.

00:49:46.226 --> 00:49:47.906
So the governor can bypass

00:49:47.906 --> 00:49:49.426
the standard public comment section

00:49:49.426 --> 00:49:51.026
and go straight to the top of the agency.

00:49:51.586 --> 00:49:53.266
Yes, but there are strict,

00:49:53.266 --> 00:49:54.466
unforgiving deadlines.

00:49:55.106 --> 00:49:57.986
To affect the crucial 2028 benchmarks,

00:49:57.986 --> 00:49:59.106
the governor must submit

00:49:59.106 --> 00:50:00.786
this formal data-driven request

00:50:00.786 --> 00:50:03.026
by February 1st, 2027.

00:50:03.026 --> 00:50:04.946
What exactly should they be asking for?

00:50:04.946 --> 00:50:06.786
The specific ask being championed

00:50:06.786 --> 00:50:08.146
by several congressional leaders

00:50:08.146 --> 00:50:09.346
and policy experts

00:50:09.346 --> 00:50:10.626
is for the governor to request

00:50:10.626 --> 00:50:11.506
a stabilization of

00:50:11.506 --> 00:50:13.586
Puerto Rico's average geographic adjustment,

00:50:13.586 --> 00:50:14.466
the AGA,

00:50:14.466 --> 00:50:16.546
at a minimum floor of 0.7 year.

00:50:16.546 --> 00:50:18.706
And that 0.70 AGA

00:50:18.706 --> 00:50:20.546
acts as the bridge over the gap.

00:50:20.546 --> 00:50:21.266
Exactly.

00:50:21.266 --> 00:50:22.226
It freezes the cuts

00:50:22.226 --> 00:50:23.426
and stabilizes the funding

00:50:23.426 --> 00:50:26.706
across that brutal 2028-2032 gap.

00:50:26.706 --> 00:50:27.826
It stops the slow bleed

00:50:27.826 --> 00:50:28.466
just long enough

00:50:28.466 --> 00:50:29.666
for the real hard data

00:50:29.666 --> 00:50:30.706
from the Vieques hospital

00:50:30.706 --> 00:50:31.986
to finally enter the spreadsheet,

00:50:31.986 --> 00:50:33.186
percolate through the audits,

00:50:33.186 --> 00:50:34.466
and take over permanently.

00:50:34.466 --> 00:50:35.826
So you fight on two fronts.

00:50:35.826 --> 00:50:37.426
You set up the geographic solution

00:50:37.426 --> 00:50:39.026
on the ground in Vieques

00:50:39.026 --> 00:50:40.466
while simultaneously fighting

00:50:40.466 --> 00:50:42.546
the administrative battle in Washington

00:50:42.546 --> 00:50:43.666
to buy the time you need

00:50:43.666 --> 00:50:45.026
for the solution to work.

00:50:45.026 --> 00:50:45.506
Wow.

00:50:45.506 --> 00:50:46.626
Okay, let's bring this all back

00:50:46.626 --> 00:50:47.826
to where we started today.

00:50:47.906 --> 00:50:49.906
The core paradox

00:50:49.906 --> 00:50:51.026
of these two islands.

00:50:51.026 --> 00:50:52.306
The tale of two islands.

00:50:52.306 --> 00:50:53.346
We have this finished

00:50:53.346 --> 00:50:55.906
$85 million hurricane-proof building

00:50:55.906 --> 00:50:56.626
sitting right now

00:50:56.626 --> 00:50:57.666
on the island of Vieques.

00:50:58.386 --> 00:51:00.146
And it is two profound things

00:51:00.146 --> 00:51:01.666
at the exact same time.

00:51:01.666 --> 00:51:02.786
First and foremost,

00:51:02.786 --> 00:51:03.906
it is a life-saving

00:51:03.906 --> 00:51:06.146
emergency room and maternity ward

00:51:06.146 --> 00:51:08.466
for 8,000 American citizens

00:51:08.466 --> 00:51:09.426
who have endured

00:51:09.426 --> 00:51:11.026
the unimaginable trauma

00:51:11.026 --> 00:51:12.146
of lacking basic care.

00:51:12.786 --> 00:51:14.306
A place where a 13-year-old girl

00:51:14.306 --> 00:51:15.186
shouldn't have to die

00:51:15.186 --> 00:51:16.466
waiting for a ventilator.

00:51:16.466 --> 00:51:17.026
Yes.

00:51:17.026 --> 00:51:19.186
But second, it is a massive

00:51:19.186 --> 00:51:21.426
multimillion-dollar financial lever

00:51:21.426 --> 00:51:22.786
for an entire territory

00:51:22.786 --> 00:51:24.786
of 3.2 million people.

00:51:24.786 --> 00:51:26.386
It proves that the vast difference

00:51:26.386 --> 00:51:27.506
between the exorbitant wealth

00:51:27.506 --> 00:51:29.026
of Nantucket's hospitals

00:51:29.026 --> 00:51:30.226
and the compounding poverty

00:51:30.226 --> 00:51:31.826
of Puerto Rico's hospitals

00:51:31.826 --> 00:51:33.346
wasn't ever really about

00:51:33.346 --> 00:51:34.306
the physical ocean

00:51:34.306 --> 00:51:34.946
separating them

00:51:34.946 --> 00:51:35.906
from the mainland.

00:51:35.906 --> 00:51:36.946
It was purely about

00:51:37.586 --> 00:51:38.786
who had the foresight

00:51:38.786 --> 00:51:40.146
or the historical luck

00:51:40.146 --> 00:51:41.346
to place a certified

00:51:41.346 --> 00:51:42.706
IPPS hospital

00:51:42.706 --> 00:51:44.226
on the geographic playing field

00:51:44.226 --> 00:51:45.586
and who knew how to master

00:51:45.586 --> 00:51:46.626
the rules of the game.

00:51:46.626 --> 00:51:47.746
It's all about knowing

00:51:47.746 --> 00:51:48.946
how the board is set up.

00:51:48.946 --> 00:51:50.626
I want to leave you, the listener,

00:51:50.626 --> 00:51:51.986
with something to mull over today

00:51:51.986 --> 00:51:53.746
as we wrap up this deep dive.

00:51:53.746 --> 00:51:54.946
A final thought.

00:51:54.946 --> 00:51:57.186
Think about your own local hospital.

00:51:57.186 --> 00:51:58.066
Think about the care

00:51:58.066 --> 00:51:59.266
your community receives

00:51:59.266 --> 00:52:00.626
the nurses at the bedside,

00:52:00.626 --> 00:52:01.826
the equipment and the ER.

00:52:02.466 --> 00:52:04.066
How much of modern healthcare

00:52:04.066 --> 00:52:04.786
is dictated

00:52:04.786 --> 00:52:06.466
not by actual medical need

00:52:06.466 --> 00:52:08.226
or the actual cost of a syringe

00:52:08.226 --> 00:52:09.986
or the skill of a local surgeon,

00:52:10.706 --> 00:52:12.226
but by the legal definition

00:52:12.226 --> 00:52:13.266
of a zip code?

00:52:13.266 --> 00:52:14.546
It's a sobering thought.

00:52:14.546 --> 00:52:15.506
When a health system's

00:52:15.506 --> 00:52:16.306
very survival

00:52:16.306 --> 00:52:17.426
depends entirely on

00:52:17.426 --> 00:52:19.426
mastering geographic legal fictions,

00:52:20.066 --> 00:52:21.906
are we optimizing for patient care

00:52:21.906 --> 00:52:23.906
or are we just optimizing for compliance?

00:52:23.906 --> 00:52:25.666
That's the million-dollar question.

00:52:25.666 --> 00:52:27.026
So what does this all mean for you?

00:52:27.586 --> 00:52:29.986
Next time you drive past a rural clinic

00:52:29.986 --> 00:52:32.226
or a massive urban medical center,

00:52:32.226 --> 00:52:34.146
remember that there are invisible lines

00:52:34.146 --> 00:52:35.346
and federal spreadsheets

00:52:35.346 --> 00:52:37.666
dictating what happens inside those walls

00:52:37.666 --> 00:52:39.506
long before you ever walk through the doors.

00:52:40.066 --> 00:52:41.586
The machinery is complex,

00:52:41.586 --> 00:52:43.586
abstract, and deeply bureaucratic,

00:52:43.586 --> 00:52:45.026
but as we saw in VX,

00:52:45.106 --> 00:52:46.946
the outcomes are intensely,

00:52:46.946 --> 00:52:48.626
sometimes tragically human.

00:52:48.626 --> 00:52:49.346
Yes, sir.

00:52:49.346 --> 00:52:50.786
Thanks for joining us for this deep dive.

00:52:50.786 --> 00:52:51.746
We'll see you next time.

